.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.db
*.sqlite*
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
build/
dist/
# A 100MB sample sound. GitHub rejects a file this size outright, and it is a
# generated asset of the static site rather than source.
star-catcher/assets/*.wav
.gradle/
local.properties
*.apk
# ...except the repository this build ships. The store lists what the index
# names and marks each row "on device" only when the artifact is really there,
# so an APK whose index is committed but whose artifacts are not would rebuild
# into the exact bug this repository was fixed for: an index full of
# extensions, none of them installed.
!android/app/src/main/assets/repository/apk/*.apk
!repo/apk/*.apk
# ProComic is served from its own directory because it carries a different
# signing key than the one this repository advertises, and a reader refuses an
# extension whose signer does not match the anchor. Same layout, separate trust.
!repo-procomic/apk/*.apk
*.jks
*.keystore
.idea/
*.iml
.and-code/
/caches/

# Client-facing published artifacts are committed so Mihon can fetch them over
# raw.githubusercontent / Pages: repo.json, index.json/index.min.json, index.pb,
# index.shura.json and apk/*.apk. Runtime state (store *.db, /artifacts/) and
# stale top-level copies at repo/ root stay ignored.
!repo/index.json
!repo/index.min.json
!repo/index.pb
!repo/repo.json
!repo/apk/
!repo/apk/*.apk

# Deferred Pro-chan harness. It is a port of ProComicImageInterceptor v1.5.1 and
# imports PIL, which is deliberately not a project dependency (pyproject keeps
# dependencies = [] and CI installs nothing). Committed as-is it fails
# `python -m unittest discover -s tests` on a clean runner with
# ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'PIL'. It stays out of version control
# until the Pro-chan phase either declares Pillow in CI or gates the harness on
# it. Do not sweep this in with `git add -A`.
tests/test_protected_tile_decode.py

/artifacts/
Build artefacts that are part of what the app ships.
android/.kotlin/
